From e6ed1c863de659fa561c93e6af8c0ebd5c71e9c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:38:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(computer-use): cua-driver links its skill pack into
 Hermes; sync zh-Hans eviction

- computer-use.md still said, in three places, that Hermes autodetection
  is a planned cua-driver follow-up and that users must point Hermes at
  ~/.cua-driver/skills/cua-driver or symlink it. The same page's "Going
  deeper" section, the cli-commands reference and the bundled
  computer-use SKILL.md already say `cua-driver skills install` detects
  Hermes and links the pack into ~/.hermes/skills/cua-driver; trycua/cua
  shipped that ("skills: autodetect Hermes (NousResearch/hermes-agent) at
  ~/.hermes/skills", trycua/cua#1963, later "honor HERMES_HOME for skill
  links", trycua/cua#3291).
- The zh-Hans computer-use page still described screenshot eviction as
  "the Anthropic adapter keeps only the last 3 screenshots". Eviction is
  now provider-independent and limit-triggered
  (agent/image_eviction_policy.py: OUTBOUND_IMAGE_LIMIT = 20,
  OUTBOUND_IMAGE_BUDGET_BYTES = 24_000_000, batch retirement), as the
  English page says; the zh-Hans bullet now translates it.

Docs only; no behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
